25. What you should remember from this section

Keep this mental model:

AUTHENTICATION
│
├── Purpose
│     └── Identify the caller
│
├── Question
│     └── "Who are you?"
│
├── Credentials / Mechanisms
│     ├── Username + Password
│     ├── Basic Authentication
│     ├── Cookie
│     ├── JWT
│     ├── Certificate
│     └── OAuth/OIDC-based login
│
└── ASP.NET Core
      │
      ├── Authentication Scheme
      ├── Authentication Handler
      ├── ClaimsIdentity
      ├── ClaimsPrincipal
      └── HttpContext.User


And then:






Authentication
      ↓
Who are you?
      ↓
ClaimsPrincipal
      ↓
Authorization
      ↓
What can you do?
      ↓
Allow / Deny





Your BasicAuthenticationDemo specifically




Client
  ↓
Authorization: Basic Base64(username:password)
  ↓
BasicAuthenticationHandler
  ↓
Decode credentials
  ↓
Validate user
  ↓
Create Claims
  ↓
ClaimsPrincipal
  ↓
HttpContext.User
  ↓
[Authorize]
  ↓
Controller
